    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (82.24) headlining the lineup as the clear top play. Facing Ure\u00f1a, **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from an elite 0.461 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against a starter with a 4.49 xERA, making him our primary engine for power and production. Not far behind, **Junior Caminero** (78.33) offers massive upside against Scherzer; while Scherzer remains a formidable name, his 5.08 xERA indicates he is far from his prime, and the platoon advantage shifts the expected outcome firmly into **Junior Caminero**\u2019s corner. We are also capitalizing on the Alcantara matchup by deploying both **Trea Turner** (72.36) and **Kyle Schwarber** (69.60) at the top of the order; both players receive significant boosts from the #1 and #2 lineup spots, with **Trea Turner**\u2019s BvP success and **Kyle Schwarber**\u2019s consistent power profile anchoring the top of the card.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Colt Keith** (46.18), who narrowly missed the cut behind the utility spot occupied by **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (58.67). While **Colt Keith** offers solid positional versatility, he is facing the daunting task of navigating Skenes, an elite arm with a 3.11 xERA, whose high-velocity, quick-to-the-plate delivery severely limits our precious SB potential. Conversely, **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** draws a significantly softer matchup against Warren and plays in a stadium that boosts his park factor by 16%, tipping the efficiency scales in his favor. Meanwhile, we remain cautious regarding **Kazuma Okamoto** (39.47), whose score dipped below our ideal threshold due to a tough draw against Rasmussen. We are also closely monitoring **Christian Yelich** and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, as both remain in \"Lineup Pending\" status; should their confirmed positions drop in the order, we will reassess our game-cap management for the remainder of the evening.",
